WEBVTT

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.620
Your job as character team leader

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.690
is to understand the graphical direction 
given by me, the art director,

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.710
and keep the character 
models in line with it.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:14.820
Okay.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.780
Also, to attend the meetings 
to coordinate with the other teams.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.820
But I'll be at those, too, so you can relax.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:25.000
R-Right...

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:29.920
Okay!

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:33.590
U-Um, Yun-chan...

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.430
Yes?

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.010
How's your progress going?!

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:13.350
I-I believe tomorrow's the deadline. 
Do you think you'll make it?

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.860
Yes, I'll be fine.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:19.070
Okay... Do your best...

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.870
R-Right...

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.060
A-Aoba-chan!

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:23.880
Yes?

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.000
Progress...?

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.970
Um... I'm sorry!

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:32.630
I spent so much time on the character designs
that I fell behind on my 3D work.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:36.380
Could I ask for two more days?

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:37.700
Okay...

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:41.150
Then... do your best.

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:43.720
I'm sorry! One day is enough!

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:44.470
Huh?

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:48.370
W-Well, Yagami-san never let me 
get away with it just like that,

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:51.040
so I got used to fudging the numbers.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.620
I see...

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:53.880
I'm sorry.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.320
No, it's fine.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.650
Let me know if you ever need more time.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.740
Okay!

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:03.910
<i>Crap. The truth is, I'm not on pace 
to finish by tomorrow, either.</i>

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:05.890
U-Um...

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:07.290
Hifumin, time for the meeting.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:10.700
Y-Yeah, I know. Let's go.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:13.730
Aoba, I heard what you just said.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:18.860
Huh? W-Well, it's not like giving you 
an honest estimate ever worked!

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:21.510
Yeah, point taken.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:24.890
Just don't be too mean to your new leader.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.970
I won't be!

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:31.820
<i>There goes my chance to tell her.
 What do I do now?</i>

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:36.190
<i>How will Hifumi-senpai take it 
when I miss the deadline?</i>

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:40.690
<i>With Yagami-san, it'd be a slap 
on the wrist and end of story.</i>

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:46.190
Aoba-chan, what do you think of 
Hifumi-senpai as leader?

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:48.120
Huh? What do you mean?

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.610
Like, do you think she's easier 
to deal with than Yagami-san?

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:54.160
Oh, that sort of thing?

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:57.490
Well, unlike Yagami-san, 
she doesn't seem very strict.

00:03:57.490 --> 00:04:00.840
Yeah. I doubt she'd get angry 
even if we deserved it.

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:04.220
Don't tell me you fudged your ETA, too?

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.560
I-I couldn't help it!

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:09.930
We always got away with it, 
so it became second nature!

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:14.610
Still, you should tell Hifumi-senpai 
the truth, or you might make her cry.

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:15.600
Huh?

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:20.360
It's... because my leadership was lacking...

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.070
I'm sorry...

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:27.310
Oh, no! But it's already 
too late to tell her.

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:28.840
Now it's deadline or bust!

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:33.620
Things were so much easier before!

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:37.130
It's no use! I can't come up with anything!

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:39.670
Your game design work seems hard.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:43.730
Yeah... I'm having a hard 
time coming up with ideas.

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:47.190
If you'd like my input on anything, 
I'd be happy to help.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:51.430
Thanks, but I'll see what I can 
come up with on my own for now.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:03.700
The last time I stayed this late alone 
must've been when I was still new.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:09.650
Hello?

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:11.490
Oh, Mom?

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:14.540
Yeah, I'm thinking I'll stay overnight.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:17.390
Huh? Miu and Ren's breakfast?

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:19.780
Wasn't it your turn to make it tomorrow?

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.200
You have work?

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:26.650
Oh, fine, I'm heading home. Jeez.

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:30.300
So much for that.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:39.940
Th-That's dangerous!

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.350
Now hurry up and get changed.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:44.570
Yun-neechan!

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:46.570
I can't find my pencil box.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.100
I told you to get ready the night before.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.950
I did! But...

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:55.660
But I wanted to draw! So I...

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:59.800
You made him cry, Yun-neechan!

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.920
Oh, jeez!

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:07.030
Good morning.

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:09.620
G-Good morning...

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:12.840
Do you think... you'll be 
able to submit the models?

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:17.430
I'm sorry, I don't think so.

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.440
Huh? Oh...

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:25.940
I was going to come in early, honestly, 
but a few things came up, and...

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:30.000
It's okay. I don't think 
you're slacking off.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.950
But why don't I help you figure 
out what caused the delay?

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.640
There's no problem with the quality...

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.290
Was the work simply time-consuming?

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:42.460
Yes, uh...

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:46.210
<i>Truth is, I knew I wasn't going 
to finish to begin with.</i>

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:47.890
Oh, I've got it!

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:48.610
Huh?

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:50.650
By the looks of your workspace,

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:53.890
you haven't set up many 
handy shortcuts, have you?

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:56.390
I'll send you my usual configuration.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:01.300
R-Right... Thanks...

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:07.800
<i>Gosh. Far from being crestfallen, 
she worried about my needs first.</i>

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:12.230
<i>Meanwhile, I was worried about 
some imaginary scenario.</i>

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:18.990
I actually knew I'd be 
a day late to begin with.

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:19.870
Huh?

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:24.500
And yet I turned around and lied to you.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.250
Please, reprimand me!

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.490
B-But it doesn't bother me at all...

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:33.010
It bothers me! I'll feel better if you do.

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:36.590
<i>R-Reprimand her? What should I do?</i>

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.150
<i>But...</i>

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:43.270
<i>I know! If I just get into 
character, like when I cosplay...</i>

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:48.540
How naughty of you to lie to me.

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:49.740
Bad girl.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:50.240
Huh?

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.640
Where's your apology?

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:55.610
I-I'm shorry...

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:57.790
Why did you lie to me?

00:07:58.250 --> 00:07:59.790
Let's hear it.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:01.460
W-Well...

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:02.890
Good morni—

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:06.750
I got carried away!

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.380
All I did was ask her to reprimand me!

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:13.880
So fishmen kigurumis in the water, huh?

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:18.200
Yes! Put it on, and you can 
move freely through the water,

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:21.810
but struggle to move on land... or something.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:25.900
I wonder if you can't better utilize 
the water environment somehow.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:27.970
That's the thing, isn't it?

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:33.920
Slow movement and the inability to breathe 
are standard drawbacks of water levels.

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.120
That's why I came up with the fishmen.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:40.370
But you can't just negate the drawbacks 
without some kind of trade-off.

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.320
Trade-off?

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:44.940
Like how wearing glasses halves my cuteness!

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:48.880
Oh, like how a kappa's weakness 
is the plate on its head!

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:48.880
<b>Weakness</b>

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.880
Right. But I think you can do better.

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:57.100
You might find that just talking it 
out like this can inspire you.

00:08:57.690 --> 00:08:59.570
Have you tried discussing it with anyone?

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:02.140
Well, no. This is my job.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:05.730
Oh, don't have so much pride 
over something so silly.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:08.390
Suzukaze-kun's the character designer,

00:09:08.390 --> 00:09:11.400
and Iijima-kun is an expert on
monsters and animals.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:14.300
There's no shame in relying on them.

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:20.660
But if I rely on Yun, she's going 
to think that I'm useless.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.870
Nor do I want to look needy 
in front of Aoba-chan...

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.020
What about me?

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:27.500
No, it's nothing! Nothing at all!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.300
Oh, okay. Just checking.

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:37.380
Um, Aoba-chan...

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:39.810
Oh, and also Yun.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:42.040
Could I get your input on something?

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:44.140
"Also"? Was I an afterthought?

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:46.520
Come on, I'm sorry, okay?

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:50.140
Underwater mechanics?

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:51.180
Yeah.

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:56.110
I'm planning to design each species 
to showcase its unique features.

00:09:57.560 --> 00:09:58.970
Wh-What is this?

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:00.620
It's just a concept!

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:04.870
But without arms or legs, 
she wouldn't be able to attack.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.620
Then what about something 
like a hammerhead shark?

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:11.120
The "hammer" is for its eyes, 
but we could make it like a blade.

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:13.560
Yeah, that sounds super strong!

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:16.800
Then we could also have 
a spiky one, like a pufferfish.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:19.720
And a sea slug one could be creepy but cool!

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:21.330
How about a turban shell?

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.330
<i>She was right.</i>

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:23.810
<i>The ideas just keep coming!</i>

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:23.810
We seem to keep picking small sea life.

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:26.930
Then what about a giant whale?

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:32.310
Aoba-chan, a whale's flukes 
are horizontal, not vertical.

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:34.380
Oh, yeah.

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:36.340
You know a lot about these things, Yun.

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:37.240
Huh?

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:42.140
O-Of course I do! I haven't been making 
monsters this whole time for nothing!

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:45.160
But what would the trade-off be?

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:47.050
That's true.

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:52.410
We may have changed how she attacks, 
but it's effectively the same as the fishmen.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:10:59.720
Actually, the first one was perfect!

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:00.720
Huh?

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:01.830
This.

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:03.870
But she won't be able to fight like that.

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:05.390
She doesn't have to.

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:09.100
Using stealth to progress is also 
part of the game's style.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:14.480
And if she wants to fight, she can 
just take off the fish kigurumi.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.480
But then she'll move sluggishly 
and won't be able to breathe.

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:23.310
She might be able to fight off one enemy,
but if she were to get surrounded...

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:26.240
I see! That sounds thrilling.

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:29.210
Exactly! Underwater thrills!

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:33.460
This is amazing! Who knew 
we'd figure this out so quickly?

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:37.590
I honestly thought I'd look inept, 
asking for advice.

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:40.340
But you really helped me out. Thanks!

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.180
Come on, you can always talk to us.

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:43.250
She's right!

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:44.940
But we'd better get equal credit.

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:46.280
Seriously?

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:48.410
Kidding, kidding.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:53.720
I see. It's quite thrilling. I like it.

00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:55.220
That was pretty fast.

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:57.860
Once I asked for input, 
the ideas started flowing!

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:00.490
The next job should be a piece of cake!

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:04.990
<i>I just hope she doesn't get too cocky...</i>

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:12.120
Aoba-chan...

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:15.640
We're going to need those new designs soon,

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:18.840
or the character team won't 
have anything to do...

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:20.930
Are they coming along?

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:24.230
I'm so sorry! 
Please give me a bit more time!

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:25.970
How many days do you need?

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:28.720
I'm actually not sure...

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:30.970
No, it's okay...

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:32.650
Now hold on!

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:40.180
True, she looks like a mean old lady, 
but as the queen and final boss?

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:41.490
Yeah, I know...

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:45.410
Do you have a clear vision of the queen?

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:48.470
An artist needs to have that 
more than anything else.

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:52.550
For example, even something like this...

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:59.770
Never mind. If I give you an answer, 
you'll just draw it like that.

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:02.270
You'll have to keep puzzling it out, Aoba.

00:13:02.270 --> 00:13:03.970
Okay.

00:13:04.390 --> 00:13:07.640
But if I don't hurry, 
the character team's schedule...

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:13.370
Then I'll design some background characters 
to give the character team some work.

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:14.890
Figure this out in the meantime.

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:18.740
What?! You're going to do grunt 
work like that, Yagami-san?

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:23.280
Well, it'll be fun to get back to basics, 
so I don't mind.

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:26.920
You've got your extension, 
so I expect results.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.320
Way to put on the pressure...

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.550
How's it going?

00:13:34.550 --> 00:13:35.830
Toyama-san...

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:41.130
Oh, this queen looks like one of the 
clients that I'm about to go meet.

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:43.380
Huh? Is she scary?

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:45.770
A little.

00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:49.090
But she's a good person once you talk to her.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:50.670
I see...

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:57.100
Do you like this queen, Aoba-chan?

00:13:57.450 --> 00:14:00.690
Huh? That's a good question.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:04.380
She's the only human character 
other than the protagonist, Peco,

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:07.720
and she's ruling over the 
plushies with fear, right?

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:11.160
I've been wondering why she'd do that.

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:16.450
Maybe I'm having trouble designing her 
because I don't understand her appeal!

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:17.870
That might be.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:22.110
I need to find something about 
her that I can personally enjoy!

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:25.880
<i>First, I should find out 
everything about the queen.</i>

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:28.430
Hello, Hazuki-san.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:30.640
Hey. What's up?

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:34.620
I wanted to find out more 
about the final boss, the queen.

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:36.850
Do you have some time right now?

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:38.070
Sure.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:43.150
So the queen must have been 
born in the human world, right?

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:47.610
Yes, she'll probably be from 
present-day Europe like Peco.

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:51.320
Did she come to the world of 
plushies alone, like Peco did?

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:54.090
We're still working out the details,

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:57.500
but the world might actually 
have been created by the queen.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.630
Perhaps life was unkind to her,

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:02.350
which made her retreat into her shell,

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:06.630
and now, in a world where she's the 
only human, she stews in her loneliness.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:08.430
Loneliness...

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:11.890
So her loneliness makes her 
lash out at others?

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:15.600
It definitely makes it hard 
for her to be nice to people.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:19.080
She stays holed up in her castle every day

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:22.620
bossing around the helpless 
plushies to suit her selfish whims.

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:27.230
So when she meets fellow human Peco, 
maybe she wants to be friends?

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:31.740
But she might not know how to 
make friends, and bully her instead.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:33.940
She sounds like a child.

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:37.010
Oh, that's good! Why don't 
we make her a child, then?

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:39.670
Huh? You mean she doesn't 
have to be an adult?!

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:42.620
Yeah. If it's a good idea, 
we'll make it work.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:48.610
Let's see... The queen was a sickly little 
girl who lived in a certain town.

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:52.180
Her room was filled with 
the plushies that she adored.

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:56.280
It was this girl who created the world 
that Peco wanders into.

00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:58.140
Why did she wander in?

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:02.640
Maybe one of the plushies, 
out of concern for the girl, lured her in.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:08.080
The plushies love the queen 
but also worry about her.

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:12.980
But they can't ease the queen's 
loneliness because they're plushies.

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:15.170
They want Peco to be friends with her.

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:19.740
Yes! And so Peco becomes 
the balm for the queen's heart.

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:22.610
I see! Thank you so much!

00:16:23.270 --> 00:16:26.250
Yagami manages to come up 
with her designs alone,

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:33.170
but you should just figure out 
what works for you, Suzukaze-kun.

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:35.800
Hmm...

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:38.230
A sickly girl...

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:41.620
And so lonely and pouty that 
you want to help her...

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.020
I think I like this girl.

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:52.440
<b>Some days later</b>

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:52.440
I'm finished!

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:55.070
That took a while.

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:57.090
I'm very sorry about that.

00:16:57.090 --> 00:16:57.950
But...

00:16:58.670 --> 00:17:00.200
the results were worth it!

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:03.600
Thank you!

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:06.840
By the way, how would you 
have drawn her, Yagami-san?

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:11.560
Me? Well, if it were me...

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:14.220
Something like this?

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:20.180
H-How can you draw something so good 
this quickly? Is this just to show me up?

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:22.470
You're the one who asked!

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:28.120
I'm still no match for Yagami-san...

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:30.840
<b>Nenecchi, Hotarun (3)
I'm coming home! So do you guys want to go
somewhere together on your days off? 
Fairies Team
Hajime sent a sticker
Hifumi
Thank you!
Nenecchi
Aaaaaaah!!!! {M: lol I was thinking about excluding the actual messages until I saw Nenecchi's message}</b>

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:32.210
<b>Hotarun
It's just about dinner time here, so I'm eating~</b>

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:33.740
<b>Today
Hotarun
I'm coming home! So do you guys want to go somewhere together on your days off?</b>

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:33.740
Hotarun!

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:35.320
I'm back.

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:39.230
Oh, you seem happy. 
Did your design go through?

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:41.740
Oh, well, that's part of it.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:46.000
A friend I went to high school with 
is coming back from studying abroad.

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.580
Studying abroad? That's impressive.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:49.330
Where was she?

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:53.340
France! Oh, I have a photo of her, too.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.780
This is from our graduation.

00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:57.720
Oh, you're all so cute.

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:01.270
She's really good at art.

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:05.060
She taught me lots of fundamentals, 
among other things...

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:06.020
Huh?

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:08.980
It's nothing like that! That's 
how they greet people in France,

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:12.270
so we were joking around 
and took a picture...

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:18.200
And that's how my boss saw 
the picture of me being kissed.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:22.880
It's nothing to be embarrassed about. 
That's just their culture.

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:24.580
All you do is...

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:28.410
Don't do that so suddenly!

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.720
You're awfully quiet, Nenecchi.

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:35.260
Huh? Well, I mean...

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:39.670
Y-You're having fun 
with this, aren't you?!

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:41.710
This is cross-cultural communication.

00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:44.930
B-But kissing while naked is...

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:48.180
O-Oh, right. Sorry...

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:54.610
So the naked part still embarrasses you?

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:55.880
Payback time!

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:00.910
Aocchi?! That tickles!

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:04.660
Take that, and that, and that!

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:05.910
<i>Wow! Aocchi finds her opponent's 
weakness and goes straight for it!</i>

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:08.000
<i>She's terrifying!</i>

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:09.910
Nenecchi!

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:13.870
F-Forcefully doing stuff like 
that is a crime, you know...

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:16.870
It's just a greeting, so it's fine!

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:18.260
Hey, wait!

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:20.880
Fine, two can play at this!

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:23.850
Hey! Don't touch me there!

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:25.810
We're just physically bonding!

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:33.810
Hotarun passed out!

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:39.670
Are you okay?

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:43.700
I guess I haven't changed.

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.770
Sorry, I got carried away.

00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:48.510
Just like always.

00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:52.370
When I see you two smile, 
it reminds me of high school.

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:57.690
It's already been a year. A lot's happened.

00:19:57.690 --> 00:20:01.260
Is Nenecchi still working part-time 
at your company, Aocchi?

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:02.940
Not anymore.

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:07.340
But I think she needs 
to find what <i>she</i> wants to do,

00:20:07.340 --> 00:20:09.350
rather than worry about me.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:12.020
She'll be fine. You know her.

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:13.770
You think so?

00:20:15.010 --> 00:20:16.270
Is your job fun?

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:17.640
It is.

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:21.080
Everyone at work is nice.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:25.700
There are plenty of challenges, 
but that's part of the fun.

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:29.790
Though going to art school with you 
might have been fun, too.

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:34.220
What are you talking about? 
You definitely would've regretted it, Aocchi.

00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:37.400
Yeah, you're probably right.

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:44.200
I'm glad. You're pressing 
onward without any regrets.

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:46.670
You're always so kind, Hotarun.

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:50.130
If we switched places, I doubt 
I'd support you as wholeheartedly.

00:20:50.130 --> 00:20:51.940
That's not true.

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:53.070
You know...

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:58.440
My dream from high school came true.

00:20:58.970 --> 00:21:04.740
But that dream turned out to be just the 
first step on a staircase that stretches on.

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:06.490
Is the top in sight?

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:07.780
I'll make it there.

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:13.750
But you know, all I had before 
was this nebulous aspiration—

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:17.310
exactly the sort of thing you'd call a dream.

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:19.300
But now I have something concrete.

00:21:19.300 --> 00:21:20.980
So more like a goal?

00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:23.010
Yeah! Something like that!

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:28.780
But whenever I see my boss, 
I realize just how far off that goal is.

00:21:29.540 --> 00:21:30.640
I'm back!

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:33.640
Ta-da! Bought some ice cream 
at the convenience store.

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:36.850
But we just ate! We're going to get fat.

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:38.570
But they looked so good!

00:21:38.570 --> 00:21:39.270
I mean—

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:44.460
H-Hotarun passed out, so I thought 
she might want something cold!

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:46.190
Oh? A likely story.

00:21:46.190 --> 00:21:47.600
I bet that was an afterthought.

00:21:47.600 --> 00:21:49.280
Was not!

00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:54.080
Uh, Hotarun?

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:56.590
I was actually just craving some.

00:21:56.590 --> 00:21:59.290
You're so nice, Hotarun. Here.

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:00.670
Thanks.

00:22:01.010 --> 00:22:03.730
Aocchi doesn't want to get fat, 
so none for her.

00:22:03.730 --> 00:22:04.590
What?!

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:06.300
Hey, that's not fair!

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:07.980
Is too fair!
